<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00970</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3c9b31f2-5983-4957-bc77-74ece101822c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="2f2b306f-ec13-4402-8bf8-7c7b9873191b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0"> <!--Q#1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d5a76d94-cf2d-48b0-bf90-ab0135ae6830" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-40">
    <problem>
      <para> Evaluate \(\frac{140-20}{9-12}\) mentally. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac{140-20}{9-12}=\frac{120}{-3}=-40\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b7468d6e-f613-4347-80db-20b285dee5e0" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="7">
    <problem>
      <para> Find the slope of the line that goes through the points \((1,-3)\) and \((2,4)\).:</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{4-(-3)}{2-1}=\frac{7}{1}=7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e74a4667-56d7-487c-8a3c-d89ccc72b044" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y = -\\frac{1}{4}x + 3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y = \\frac{1}{4}x + 3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y = 3x + \\frac{1}{4}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(4x - y = -3 \\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Write the equation of the line in slope-intercept form that goes through \((0,3)\) and has a slope of \(\frac14\) .</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y = \frac{1}{4}x + 3\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="78162944-7ce7-4725-9eeb-2dfeb4a0e30a" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y+1 = - \frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y = -\\frac{1}{2}x -1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y+1 = - \\frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y = -\\frac{1}{2}x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2x + y = 0\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Write the equation of the line that passes through \((2,-1)\) and has a slope of \(-\frac{1}{2}\) in point-slope form.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y+1 = - \frac{1}{2}(x - 2)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f90277af-e3c7-4ab4-9630-52aad43c5c02" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(6x - 3y = 3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(5x + 2y = 9\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(6x - 3y = 3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-4x + 5y = 9\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{1}{2}x + 3y = 8\\)&quot;,&quot;\\(5x + 2y = 9\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(5y + 2x = 10\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> <emphasis>Select two</emphasis> equations that are correctly in standard form.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\) </para>
      <para>\(6x - 3y = 3\) and \(5x + 2y = 9\) are in standard form because they are of the form \(Ax + By = C\).</para>
      <para>They do not have any fractions or decimals and start with a positive coefficient.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q#6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d6d45287-acba-4ec5-be73-10739e3a7b6f" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4x-y=2">
    <problem>
      <para> Write \(y = 4x - 2\) in standard form. Hint: Do not include spaces in your answer.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(4x -y = 2\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y &amp;=&amp; 4x - 2\\ y - 4x &amp;=&amp; 4x - 4x - 2\\ -4x + y &amp;=&amp; -2 \\-1(-4x + y &amp;=&amp; -2) \\4x - y &amp;=&amp; 2\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.7.3 and 4.7.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8c745b6e-b2ec-4fc2-92a8-44e56278d896" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="y=-2x+14">
    <problem>
      <para> Write the equation \(y-4=-2(x-5)\) in slope-intercept form. Hint: Do not include spaces in your answer.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y=-2x+14\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-4&amp;=&amp;-2(x-5) \\ y-4&amp;=&amp;-2x+10\\ y&amp;=&amp;-2x+10+4\\ y&amp;=&amp;-2x+14\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.7.3 and 4.7.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f9c71f6e-98ce-4efa-82bd-e267e9dd980e" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para> Find the slope of the line between the points \((3,-1)\) and \((2,-4)\). </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3</para>
      <para>\(m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}=\frac{-4-(-1)}{2-3}=\frac{-3}{-1}=3\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8f1c5941-2186-4b07-b376-5ee300a9f4b6" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3x-y=-17">
    <problem>
      <para> Write the equation \(y-2=3(x+5)\) in standard form. Hint: Do not include spaces in your answer. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(3x-y=-17\)</para>
      <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-2&amp;=&amp;3(x+5)\\y-2&amp;=&amp;3x+15\\y-2-3x&amp;=&amp;3x-3x+15\\y-3x-2&amp;=&amp;15\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;15+2\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;17\\-1-3x+y&amp;=&amp;17\\3x-y&amp;=&amp;-17\end{array}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.7.3 and 4.7.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q#10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7fe6a5ff-1a71-478a-932d-5e5d7b0e7d4b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3">
    <problem>
      <para> Evaluate \(\frac{36-48}{10-14}\) mentally. </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3</para>
      <para>\(\frac{36-48}{10-14} =\frac{-12}{-4}=3\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.7.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
